  "description": "QAVSOX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C88 H78 Dy6 N24 O32,C88 H78 Dy6 N24 O32,C2 H6 O1,5(C1 H4 O1),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy7 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.770-4.911 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.01-167.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(OAc)3(μ3-CO3)2(L)5(HL)(MeOH)2]·4H2O·5MeOH·EtOH (H2L = (E)-N'-(2-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzylidene)pyrazine-2-carbohydrazide). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
